Feature: Daily Pivot Bias
  Primary timeframe: 1h

  # Demonstrates the 0.52 INC3 pivot-point primitives end-to-end:
  #  - Go long when price reclaims the STANDARD daily pivot P (bullish bias).
  #  - Exit when price loses the daily pivot P again.
  # The pivot levels are recomputed each UTC day from the prior completed
  # day's OHLC (nachtkrapp PivotPointRule, PriceSource.CLOSE). The level
  # token (P) is symbolic — it is not a numeric period.

  Scenario: Enter long when price reclaims the daily pivot
    Given no open position
    When price_crosses_above_pivot(P)
    Then long_entry

  Scenario: Exit long when price loses the daily pivot
    Given a long position is open
    When price_crosses_below_pivot(P)
    Then long_exit
